  "blueprint_md": "# Automation blueprint: Invoice intake and validation\n\n## Process summary\n\n- **Description:** Supplier invoices arrive by email as PDF, are keyed into the ERP, matched to purchase orders and approved for payment.\n- **Owner:** Finance Operations\n- **Executions per month:** 400\n- **Steps:** 5\n- **Analysis:** <timestamp>, process version 1, rules scoring-v1, LLM ok (fake/fake-deterministic-v1)\n\n## Current state\n\n- **Monthly hours:** 95.33\n- **Monthly cost:** 1,763.67\n\n## Automation opportunities\n\nOrdered by monthly time. Suitability measures whether a step can be automated, not how much it is worth.\n\n| # | Step | Method | Human control | Decided by | Hours/month | Suitability |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---:|---:|\n| 3 | Match invoice with purchase order | HYBRID | NONE | AI | 33.33 | 80 |\n| 2 | Extract invoice fields | API_INTEGRATION | RECOMMENDED | RULES | 26.67 | 68 |\n| 5 | Approve payment | RULE_BASED | REQUIRED | RULES | 13.33 | 60 |\n| 4 | Resolve discrepancies with supplier | HYBRID | REQUIRED | AI | 12.00 | 0 |\n\n- **Match invoice with purchase order:** Input is digital structured and integration readiness is partial.\n- **Extract invoice fields:** the systems involved expose a usable integration\n- **Approve payment:** clear rules over structured digital input with few exceptions\n- **Resolve discrepancies with supplier:** Input is mixed and integration readiness is none.\n\n## Proposed architecture\n\n- Workflow engine that runs the steps in order, with retries and an audit log\n- Rules step in the workflow engine with explicit, versioned validation rules\n- API connectors to the systems already in use\n- Automated draft with a person confirming the result\n- Human review queue: flagged items wait for a decision, which is logged\n- Orchestrate the automated steps from a single workflow engine with retries\n- Route low-confidence and flagged items to a human review queue\n\n## Business impact\n\nEvery economic figure below depends on the assumptions listed after it.\n\n- **Hours freed per month:** 41.00\n- **Gross monthly savings:** 758.50\n- **Monthly tooling cost:** 50.00\n- **Net monthly savings:** 708.50\n- **Implementation cost:** 6,000.00\n- **Payback (months):** 8.47\n- **ROI at 12 months:** 42 %\n\n**Assumptions**\n\n- Implementation cost: 6,000.00\n- Monthly tooling cost: 50.00\n- Expected time reduction for step <step-1>: 50 %\n- Expected time reduction for step <step-2>: 50 %\n- Expected time reduction for step <step-3>: 50 %\n- Expected time reduction for step <step-4>: 50 %\n- 1 step(s) have no expected reduction and count as zero savings\n\n## Risks\n\n- [RULES / DATA] Extract invoice fields handles sensitive data\n- [AI / STEP] Data protection: restrict access and log processing\n- [RULES / OPERATIONAL] Resolve discrepancies with supplier depends on human judgement\n- [RULES / DATA] Approve payment handles sensitive data\n- [RULES / OPERATIONAL] Approve payment is business critical\n- [AI / STEP] Data protection: restrict access and log processing\n- [AI / OPERATIONAL] Exceptions need an owner once the happy path is automated\n\n## Human controls\n\n- **Download invoice from shared mailbox:** REQUIRED. Reviewer decision: Reviewer keeps this step manual\n- **Extract invoice fields:** RECOMMENDED. handles sensitive data\n- **Resolve discrepancies with supplier:** REQUIRED. requires human judgement\n- **Approve payment:** REQUIRED. requires human approval\n\n## Workflow specification\n\n1. Trigger: a new process execution starts\n2. Download invoice from shared mailbox: MANUAL, then wait for a person to approve before continuing\n3. Extract invoice fields: API_INTEGRATION, with a person reviewing a sample or the flagged cases\n4. Match invoice with purchase order: HYBRID\n5. Resolve discrepancies with supplier: HYBRID, then wait for a person to approve before continuing\n6. Approve payment: RULE_BASED, then wait for a person to approve before continuing\n7. End: record the outcome and the time spent for later comparison\n",
